---
id: PY-011
type: rule
family: python-reliability
title: 'eval/exec/compile first argument PY-008 cannot see'
version: 1

severity: warning
confidence: high
spectrum_position: 8

targets: [source]
file_extensions: [.py]
allowlist: ['**/test_*.py', '**/*_test.py', '**/tests/**', '**/conftest.py', '**/explain/**']

detection:
  type: ast
  ast_query: '(call) @target'

related: [PY-008]
enabled: true
opt_in: false
---

PY-008's regex reads the first token after `(` on one line, so concatenated,
formatted, f-string, and wrapped first arguments are blind. This gate-time AST
companion flags those shapes on `eval` / `exec` / `compile`, plus in-file
`from builtins import eval as X` / `compile as X` used as a call, and
`builtins.compile` / `__builtins__.compile` of a dynamic argument.

It does **not** fire on `re.compile`, `torch.compile`, or `self.compile`.
Unqualified `eval(user)` on one line stays PY-008 (save-time regex). Do not
convert PY-008 to `detection: ast`.
